So I start off with an wiz-elf-cha-mal with force bolt and knock as the
starting spells, as well as rings of regeneration and searching.  Not
so shabby.  My cat dies an early death, but that's  just so many newt
corpses I won't have eaten out from under me.

Some combo of luck and savvy gets me through to DL8, where I find a
used book store.  Among the acquired spell books I get wizard lock,
remove curse, identify, and create monster.  I use identify until I'm
up to basic divination, at which point I figure I'll tackle the Mines.

The Mines are pretty uneventful.  Find a chaotic altar in Minetown
which, with the create monster spell, puts me in pretty good standing
with my diety.  I'm also granted the gifts of Magicbane and Frost
Brand, which are much appreciated.  The only tense part of the Mines is
the bottom level where the Vampire Lords toy with me as I try to
navigate the maze.  Expeditious retreats and a wand of magic missiles
get me the luckstone and I find my way back out of the Mines.

This, by the way, is the best that I've done with a wizard.

So then I come across the first of the Sokoban levels.  I start pushing
around boulders to find that one doesn't move due to some creature
behind it.  I normally don't carry ranged weapons as a wizard as force
bolt tends to do the job for me.  That's not going to cut it here as I
don't want this boulder reduced to rubble.  So out comes Frost Bane and
I move around to find out what's been causing the trouble.

"Air elemental engulfs you!"

Ok, don't panic.  I'll just teleport out of here with that blessed
scroll of teleportation.  Then we'll see how this guy does without the
element of surprise.

"A mysterious force prevents you from teleporting!"

Oh, crap.  That's right, I'm in Sokoban.  Time to read that Air
Elemental FAQ.

... Time passes ...

Er, no polymorph, no teleport away, no charming, no taming, no slowing.
 Hmm, I do have that knock spell.  Why the heck not?  Bippity, bobbity,
*boom*.

I'm free!

"Air elemental engulfs you!"

*wham* *wham* *wham*

"You die."

The kicker is I won't even find a bones level with all those
spellbooks.  *sigh*


